.TH BIGINTZERO 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntZero, int_32ToBigInt, bigIntFromString \- initialize an unsigned big integer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "void bigIntZero(BigInt *" "a" ");"
.sp
.BI "void int_32ToBigInt(BigInt *" "a" ", uint32_t " "val" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigIntFromString(BigInt *" "a" ", const char *" "dec_str" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bigIntZero()
clears all limbs of a and sets its size to 1, representing zero.
.B int_32ToBigInt()
initializes a from val, clearing unused limbs.
Neither function requires a previously initialized destination.
.PP
.B bigIntFromString()
initializes a to zero, then parses the NUL-terminated decimal string dec_str.
Only ASCII digits 0 through 9 are accepted; signs, whitespace, and separators
are rejected.  Leading zeros are accepted.  An empty string produces zero.
The string pointer must not be NULL.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The first two functions return no value.
.B bigIntFromString()
returns 0 on success, \-1 for a non-digit character, or INT_MAX if capacity
is exceeded.  An error can leave a partial result in a.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
BigInt n;
if (bigIntFromString(&n, "4294967296") != 0)
    return 1;
printBigInt(&n);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR printBigInt (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
